Requires-Dist: intervaltree

# SigVCF

Extracts a mutation-count matrix directly from VCFs -- no upstream
matrix-generation step needed. Three matrix types, one module each,
loaded only when requested:

| `--matrix-type` | Inputs                          | Channels |
|------------------|----------------------------------|----------|
| `sbs96`          | `.vcf` + `.fasta`(`.fai`)        | 96       |
| `sbs192`         | `.vcf` + `.fasta` + `.gtf[.gz]`  | 192      |
| `dbs78`          | `.vcf` + `.fasta`                | 78       |

Everything streams: SNVs are read one VCF record at a time via
`pysam.VariantFile`, trinucleotide context is pulled from an indexed
FASTA via `pysam.FastaFile` (no genome held in RAM), and a GTF (only
needed for `sbs192`) is parsed once into an `intervaltree` index. No
network access and no bundled reference data -- built to run inside
an offline Apptainer/Singularity container on an air-gapped cluster.

## Install

```
pip install -e .
```

## Usage

```
sigvcf --matrix-type sbs96 \
    --vcf sample1.vcf sample2.vcf.gz \
    --fasta /ref/GRCh38.fa \
    --output-dir out/ \
    --output-prefix counts_myrun \
    --output-formats tab_with_index sigfit
```

```
sigvcf --matrix-type sbs192 \
    --vcf sample1.vcf \
    --fasta /ref/GRCh38.fa \
    --gtf /ref/gencode.v44.gtf.gz \
    --output-dir out/
```

```
sigvcf --matrix-type dbs78 \
    --vcf sample1.vcf \
    --fasta /ref/GRCh38.fa \
    --output-dir out/
```

Output is written as `{output-prefix}_{format}.dat` per requested
`--output-formats` entry: a tab- or comma-separated table, mutation
channels as rows (index name `Type`) and one column per `--vcf`
(named from `--sample-names` or each file's stem). This is the same
shape [SigFitBench](../SigFitBench)'s fitting-tool rules already
consume, so a matrix produced here drops straight into that pipeline
(see `SigFitBench/workflow/rules/vcf_input.smk`).

Pass `--matrix-order some_order.dat` (one channel label per line) to
reindex the output rows to match a specific reference-signature file's
row order before fitting.

## Notes on DBS78 canonicalization

The 78 channels are derived programmatically, not from a hardcoded
COSMIC table: 10 of the 16 possible reference dinucleotides are
canonical, the rest fold onto them via reverse-complementing the
(ref, alt) pair together, and the 4 reference dinucleotides that are
their own reverse complement get an extra alt-level fold. This
produces exactly 78 self-consistent channels (verified in
`sigvcf/dbs78.py`'s docstring derivation) but its exact channel
*labels* have not been cross-checked byte-for-byte against
SigProfilerMatrixGenerator's reference list -- do that before treating
counts as COSMIC-exact for downstream comparison.

## Notes on SBS192 transcribed/untranscribed classification

`sigvcf/transcript_strand.py` implements a documented simplification
of the T/U/I convention (loci overlapped by transcripts on both
strands are reported as intergenic rather than guessed). Validate
against a reference tool if exact COSMIC parity matters for your use
case.
